WHAT TESTER IS
tester is the shared working incantation: Tony and Clod both use it to try out whatever feature is in the works, so what
sits above stop() changes often and is only ever as finished as the work in flight. It is tracked in git and commits under
Tony's name like any of his WIP files. It is not a scratch file (incant++ is the only one of those).

WHAT IT DOES TODAY
It shows the firstLight form, nothing more: the clean test of show (SEQ 690).
    Start();           fire the Start rule (still the old-grammar version).
    show(firstLight);  look firstLight up by name and draw it.
    stop();            stop reading. Nothing below this line is parsed.

HOW show DOES IT
show is a bootstrap in incant/setup. On its first call it loads utilities, then hands the work to the real worker,
showForm. showForm finds the form by name in the stash (registry sTASh, built from the hand-kept list in
incant/stashList), lays out a copy of it with setFrame (the form's own definition is never changed), draws that copy to
IncantForms/PDF/output.pdf, and, with the viewer properties field on (the default), opens output.pdf in the system viewer
in the background. show puts the search list back the way it found it and returns nothing.
firstLight itself includes descriptions, so this one line exercises a form held inside another form (inside form:=...).

HOW TO USE IT
Above stop() is live and below it is dead, so moving lines across stop() turns them on and off. When Tony and Clod are
both working in tester, each moves the other's in-progress work below stop() rather than deleting it, and each looks
over tester to see what the other is up to. Anything parked below this note is someone's work waiting its turn.

CLOD'S PROBES, SEQ 726 (2026-11-21), parked for Topics/forms G3. Each ran from the repo root as its own file (copy a block out above stop() alone,
or into a scratch file; INCANT_NOVIEW=1). Results: rowProbe -- rA (height on crossing) refuses pValue / and lays out one row; rB (height on the row) lays out 4 rows of 2.
cheatProbe -- cases 1 and 2 print CHEAT (a body, and utilities' own redrawForm); its case 3 was a bad top-level spelling, replaced by d3. d3_control and d3_cheat --
